WEBVTT

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:06.190
It's so cold.

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:10.820
The only time I hate riding my
bike is when it's this cold.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:14.530
Unless I do this, the engine won't even start.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.790
It should work now.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:08.960
Today's another hot one, huh?

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:28.270
この坂を上り切ったら
kono saka o noborikittara

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:32.230
必ず見える景色が好きだって
kanarazu mieru keshiki ga suki datte

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:32.280
必ず見える景色が好きだって

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:38.410
背中に羽を持つあの子も言って笑ってた
senaka ni hane o motsu ano ko mo itte waratteta

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:42.080
ドキドキが一瞬で
dokidoki ga isshun de

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:46.160
トキメキになっていくんだなんて
tokimeki ni natteikunda nante

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:49.880
あの頃は信じられなくて
ano koro wa shinjirarenakute

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:54.840
ただ見惚れていたよ
tada mitoreteita yo

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:59.470
このスピードに乗せた体温が
kono supiido ni noseta taion ga

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:03.220
今全身で伝う　通じ合う
ima zenshin de tsutau tsuujiau

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:06.850
物語の鍵はこの手に
monogatari no kagi wa kono te ni

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:10.360
ぎゅっと強く握っているから
gyutto tsuyoku nigitteiru kara

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:14.070
感じて　応えて　風になる
kanjite kotaete kaze ni naru

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:17.740
空に溶けて海を抱きしめる
sora ni tokete umi o dakishimeru

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:21.660
新しい世界が見えるはず
atarashii sekai ga mieru hazu

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:28.750
さぁ確かめに行ってみよう
saa tashikame ni ittemiyou

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:42.390
Winter Break!!
Episode 8

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:45.810
What are you doing, Hane?

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:47.180
Hey, Onsa-chan!

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:51.150
Merry
Christmas

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:55.730
Speaking of Christmas, it's your birthday too, right?

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.650
So you'll be getting your license, right?

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:00.490
You can start driving to school before
your birthday, you know.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:03.160
I already have one.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.620
Hm? What's up with that?

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.330
It's all filled in!

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:13.000
Don't tell me it's counterfeit.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.630
Absolutely not!

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:17.340
This is a foreign license transfer!

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:21.220
There are countries that will
give you licenses for money.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:24.600
Bring them back to Japan and
get them exchanged for a full license!

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:29.390
If something can be fixed with money,
then it shall be fixed with money.

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:31.520
That's the Minowa family motto.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:35.480
Hijiri, I gotta ask you something.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:38.030
What does the yellow traffic light mean?

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:42.860
"Go straight forward into
the road you believe in!"

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.290
What are you doing?!

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:50.790
Do you have any idea how much of a pai-

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:53.370
The state may approve of it, but I don't!

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.750
Hane, what do yellow traffic lights mean?

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:59.460
"Stop, but if you're in a place

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:01.720
where you can't safely stop, keep going."

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:02.930
See?

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:05.550
Even if she doesn't understand what
she's saying, she still repeats it right.

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:08.600
That's how education in the country works.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:11.480
If you've never even taken a test,

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:13.850
you've probably never been on a bike.

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:16.860
You should probably practice before the training.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:17.980
She's right.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:20.740
Let's have you practice on school grounds.

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:22.530
That sounds good!

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:24.570
But where are we going
to get her a practice bike?

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:25.870
Let's see...

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:27.990
She could just use a bike from my place.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:30.910
In that case, I'll send Hayakawa.

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:35.080
Thank you.

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:40.960
Hijiri!

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:43.510
It's a Honda Super Cub!

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:45.380
The engine's in top shape.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:49.430
Stout and economical, it's the
best selling bike in the world!

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:51.810
The bike of the working class, huh?

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.520
What are you saying?

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:57.270
In Southeast Asia, it's a limousine
that can carry an entire family,

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.650
while also being a truck that
can carry all your luggage.

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:02.070
To most people in the world,

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:04.200
The Super Cub is the very definition of "freedom."

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:07.820
Hayakawa-san bought it from Nicoichi,

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:10.280
so it's fine if you drop it.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:12.700
There's no clutch, and only 3 speed gears.

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:15.830
It's basically easier to ride than a bicycle.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.630
I'm not bragging or anything,

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:21.420
but I've never ridden a bicycle.

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:33.980
Senpai, please hold on.

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:35.270
Don't let go yet.

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:45.320
I... I'm driving!

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:47.280
All on my own!

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:51.160
Looks like she's having fun.

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:00.840
I can do it this time.

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:04.260
Get some speed, cut the
throttle, and go into second!

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:36.120
Hijiri-chan, are you ok?

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:40.580
I'm fine.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:43.380
Your legs are wobbling.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:47.050
I think that's enough practice for today.

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:56.720
Wha... Hijiri-chan?

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:03.360
What do you plan to do with that?

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:04.270
You...

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:07.030
damned piece of junk!

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:18.370
You piece of junk, you don't belong in this age!

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:22.290
How could anyone have fun riding this piece of junk!?

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:25.670
Stop it!

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:29.090
Hayakawa-san?

00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:32.180
Super Cubs aren't pets.

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:35.390
Super Cubs are what we call punching bags.

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:41.440
Nothing else in the world can survive this abuse.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:44.360
From a beginner's irrational anger,

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:47.650
to taking hits from novices falling.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:50.740
Going beyond what it was designed for,

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:52.700
or even from bad maintenance.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:57.540
Against all this, around the world, in any age.

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:02.040
Serves you right!

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:05.540
With a complete beatdown like
this, you'll never move again!

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:07.960
It's completely dead.

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:09.840
And to prove it...

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:12.300
Look, if I hit this button it wo—

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:34.030
Why?

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:38.200
After all this, why are you still moving?

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:45.000
Y-You know, Hijiri,

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.130
we were mistaken.

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:50.630
It's alright if you have an overseas license.

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:52.050
No.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:09:00.180
I will show you I can ride it on my own, somehow.

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:02.140
Nicoichi Motors

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.100
We got rid of an old Cub,

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:08.150
and now we get to make repairs on it.

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:09.770
I might be a genius.

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:13.190
You better work hard or I'll sell you too!

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:16.030
Just kidding.

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:23.700
Dad, I get it now!

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:26.540
Bikes are just like people!

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:28.000
That's right.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.920
Bikes are just like people.

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:33.300
They don't like moving or working.

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:33.880
Huh?

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:39.090
Do you know why bikes can't stand on
their own? Why they fall all the time?

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:43.310
They just want to laze around
whenever they get the chance.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:47.230
Minowa-san.

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:49.020
Biking to school?

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.150
It was tough getting your license, wasn't it?

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:55.400
There's a license you can
get with just a written exam.

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:58.950
With this bike, all I need is a moped license.

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:00.700
That's great!

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:03.990
Nicoichi Motors' repair work is amazing!

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:07.080
Just so you know, I had nothing to do with it.

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:09.580
Actually, it kind of stands out, doesn't it?

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.840
With those training wheels.

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:17.970
Ba
kuon<i>!!</i>

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:21.970
Ba
kuon<i>!!</i>

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:26.600
TL Note: Meri Kurisumasu means Merry Christmas
Yo, Hane! Meri Kurisumasu!

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:27.850
Welcome!

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:29.770
You're the first one here.

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:30.690
Welcome!

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:33.020
TL Note: Meri Kurisumasu means Merry Christmas
Yume-chan, Meri Kurisumasu!

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:35.110
Hane, I made it.

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:36.400
TL Note: Meri Kurisumasu means Merry Christmas
Meri Kurisumasu!

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:38.030
I have made it.

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:39.780
TL Note: Meri Kuri is equivalent to "Merry X-Mas"
Meri Kuri, Hijiri-chan.

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:42.870
Hijiri, did you actually come here on that Cub?

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:44.240
Of course I did.

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:47.330
The people I drive by leave tons of room for me.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:50.880
So this is how an outlaw lives, huh?

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:54.300
Target reached destination.

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:56.130
Returning home now.

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:02.140
Anyone would make room
with those two following her.

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:09.390
Cheers!

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:12.230
We all crossed the finish line
at almost the exact same time, right?

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:15.230
Even though Rin's not a
member, she ended up winning.

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:19.650
Hey, Rin, wanna buy a
Cyclone with your prize money?

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:21.070
I'll take care of it.

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:24.030
Katanas look best with
their normal two mufflers.

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:26.240
Why would I change its perfect style?

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:27.830
Did you get that, Hane?

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:28.950
Sure did.

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:31.040
You're talking about muffler
manufacturers, right?

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:33.420
Wow, you know what Yoshimura is?

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:34.460
Yup.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:39.630
Speaking of that, even in
third grade, I still believed in Santa.

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:42.130
Me, too! Until third grade!

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:45.800
I hope Santa-san gets here soon.

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:48.310
Santa-san!

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:52.850
Huh?

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:57.110
Onee-chan, since you're going to
be in highschool next year, I should tell you...

00:11:57.440 --> 00:12:00.950
I couldn't believe Santa was actually Yume.

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:03.320
By "third grade," you mean
third year of middle school?

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:05.780
I know what that's like, too.

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:06.780
In third grade,

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:10.540
my class split into the "people who believe
in Santa" and the "people who don't."

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:14.960
Everyone who believed in Santa
got pressured into not believing, with only me left.

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:17.840
But I was certain.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:20.090
For being a good girl,

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:23.630
you get a Tamiya 1/12-scale Katana.

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:27.850
Because he knew what I wanted every year.

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:30.100
Please, Santa-san,

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:32.770
tell my classmates that you're real.

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:34.810
Sorry, Rin-chan.

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:39.230
The truth is that your dad asked
me to pretend to be Santa.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.530
I believed you!

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:44.780
Liar! Monster! Devil!

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:47.370
You got angry at the wrong person.

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:51.450
The Santa-san who came to my house
rode a reindeer-driven sleigh!

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:52.620
Is that some new thing?

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:57.210
That Santa flew in from Denmark,

00:12:57.210 --> 00:12:59.840
on a four-reindeer sleigh.

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:05.590
Then he proves his identity as the real Santa,

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:07.010
gives his gifts,

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:09.720
and moves on to deliver gifts to
children in the next nation.

00:13:10.260 --> 00:13:11.520
Uh, what?

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:13.890
I knew it, there is a Santa!

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:16.770
Yes, hello?

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:19.020
Yes... I see.

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:22.900
Sorry, Hane. I gotta go.

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.610
Work called.

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:28.700
Since there's no one in today, I get payed double.

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:30.120
What about presents?

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:32.290
Keep what's left for me.

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:35.790
Let's draw lots, then.

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:37.210
3!

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:38.460
I got 4.

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:39.330
2.

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:41.090
Raimu-senpai got 5.

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:43.210
Okay, I got 1, so I'll start.

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:46.090
Whose present is this?

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:49.340
Geh! It's a Rin!

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:51.310
A handmade doll of herself?!

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:53.810
Why the hell would she even think of this?!

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:55.020
It's cute, though.

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:57.020
Jesus, it's irritating me!

00:13:57.020 --> 00:14:00.480
How conceited do you have to be to make this?!

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:11.280
Safe! It didn't break.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:15.250
Her head fell off!

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:17.540
Done!

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:21.380
Glued, and reinforced with tape.

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:25.710
But, it's hard not to see someone
with a cast after an accident.

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:27.130
How ominous.

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:30.050
Okay.

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:32.550
Hey, where's that Santa costume?

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:34.220
Why, Onee-chan?

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:39.060
She told us to wait for her.

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:43.520
But Christmas presents should
be delivered on Christmas.

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:49.110
Rin-chan, here comes Santa,

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:51.120
on a four-reindeer sleigh!

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:02.290
It's Quick Pizza!

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:04.630
Your pizza is here!

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:06.210
It's Santa-san!

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:07.460
Santa-san's here!

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:08.630
No it's not, Jirou.

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:12.510
She's only dressed like Santa.
She's just delivering pizza.

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:15.600
There's no such thing as Santa, anyway.

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:16.680
Oh.

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:17.980
Wait a second.

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:21.560
Why do you think there isn't a Santa?

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:23.310
I <i>am</i> Santa.

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:24.770
Got a problem? Huh?!

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:26.440
N-No, ma'am.

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:28.190
Good.

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:30.650
You're such a good boy.

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:38.290
Where in God's name is Rin-chan?

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:42.420
Wait, have we met before?

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:46.670
Those are strange clothes.

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:49.880
You say that while wearing a Santa costume?

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:51.840
Oh, you mean this?

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:53.760
This is a Santa Claus costume.

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:07.020
Finally finished.

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:09.360
I wonder if the party ended already.

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:14.820
TL Note: Meri Kurisumasu means Merry Christmas
Meri Kurisumasu, Rin-chan!

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:18.160
Hane! Why are you wearing that?

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:20.540
Since you were a good girl this year,

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:23.920
Santa-san has a present for you.

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:27.130
This is from the gift exchange.

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:29.380
You came all the way here to bring it to me?

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:31.800
It's...

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:35.430
Yup. A Yoshimura muffler.

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:36.680
A pun?

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:38.720
Nice, isn't it? I made it.

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:42.520
It's so dumb it's funny.

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:47.060
Alright, Santa's going back to the North Pole.

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:49.610
It's snowing.

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:51.440
It's a white Christmas!

00:16:56.950 --> 00:17:02.580
I guess <i>this</i> kind of Yoshimura is alright.

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:10.880
She looks the same.

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:12.210
Is this a bad omen?

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:17.140
Wait, this patch doesn't even say Yoshimura!

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:22.060
What the hell is this?!

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:27.480
Happy New Year!

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:30.320
Great Luck

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:31.820
I got Great Luck!
Great Luck

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:32.990
So-so Luck.

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:33.780
Good Luck.

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:35.360
Bad Luck.

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:36.990
You drew that one?

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:38.410
Total shock.

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:40.830
I'll buy you takoyaki, so cheer up.

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:42.160
Really?

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:43.910
Itadakimasu!

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:49.380
Huh? There was no octupus in it.

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:51.130
Huh? Let me see.

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:55.670
There was a lot in mine!

00:17:55.920 --> 00:17:57.130
Can I have one?

00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:58.590
Me, too.

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:02.810
It's crispy on the outside
and gooey on the inside.

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:04.350
And the octopus is chewy.

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:05.810
Mine had two octupus bits!

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:09.480
I guess mine just didn't have any.

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:11.060
Huh?

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:13.030
No octopus in this one, either.

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:15.400
Is it because of the fortune I drew?

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:18.990
All right, let's go home and get ready.

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:19.660
Huh?

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:20.990
For the first sunrise.

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:23.240
We're going to Inubousaki to see it.

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:26.500
Biking on a winter highway!

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:30.750
Freedom on the freeway!

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:41.510
I couldn't find my Super Four key,
so I used my spare key.

00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:44.100
I guess that fortune you drew was no joke.

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:47.520
Hijiri's sidecar is practically a car.

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:49.190
Hayakawa-san is amazing.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:51.730
I bet winter in Japan is like summer to him,

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:54.110
compared to Siberia's cold weather.

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:56.610
Motorcycles are tough, huh?

00:18:56.610 --> 00:19:00.820
Hey, why do you call bikes "autobikes?"

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:03.990
Because bicycles are also called "bikes,"

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:06.790
so foreigners would understand "autobike," too.

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:09.330
It's "motorcycle" in English.

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:10.210
Huh?!

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:13.630
Crap, we might not make it in
time for the sunrise.

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:14.630
Let's hurry.

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:22.640
The wind is really stinging my hands.

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:25.930
Time to fire up my secret weapon,
electric hand warmer grips!

00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:33.980
Huh?

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:36.400
My hand warmer grips are getting colder.

00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:38.360
What?

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:41.320
My heated innerwear is getting colder, too!

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:44.070
Wait, guys! It's too cold!

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:47.240
I can't keep up with you!

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:48.750
Don't sweat it, Hane.

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:51.160
We'll see you at the Inubousaki Lighthouse.

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:52.500
What?!

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:54.630
You're leaving me behind?

00:19:56.880 --> 00:19:59.920
It's so cold!

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:16.900
I'm defrosting...

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:19.440
To think engine heat would be so precious

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:22.570
when there's no escape from the cold.

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:25.120
I never knew.

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:32.620
I should have quit when I got
Bad Luck as my fortune.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:36.840
I should've quit when
I couldn't find my key.

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:40.670
The wind is so cold. My tears won't stop.

00:20:40.670 --> 00:20:42.420
My nose keeps running.

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:46.550
My breath is clouding my visor, so I can't see.

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:51.850
Motorcycles are...

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:09.530
"The one you are waiting for will come."

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:11.660
Great Luck really does work!

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:15.080
I made it.

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:26.680
Bikes sure are a lot of work.

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:29.350
You lose several times more energy

00:21:29.350 --> 00:21:32.310
just traveling the same distance.

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:35.600
"Bikes", more like, "Yikes."

00:21:43.860 --> 00:21:48.160
I bet it's "autobike" because
you're <i>awed</i> twice as much!

00:22:09.090 --> 00:22:10.800
buon!  buon!  buon!  buon!  buoon!

00:22:10.930 --> 00:22:13.770
FURU SUROTTORU de iin janai?

00:22:13.890 --> 00:22:15.600
buon!  buon!  buon!  buon!  buoon!

00:22:15.680 --> 00:22:18.480
todorokima~su, bakuon!!

00:22:18.810 --> 00:22:21.020
joushi koukousei BAIKU nori

00:22:21.060 --> 00:22:23.650
kaze o kiri hashiri dashichau yo  (buoon!)

00:22:23.650 --> 00:22:25.320
METTO o kabutte  (buoon!)

00:22:25.360 --> 00:22:28.150
hora ne HEASUTAIRU pettanko

00:22:28.280 --> 00:22:29.700
ii koto nashi kamo?

00:22:29.700 --> 00:22:32.780
itsudatte MENTE de kigen o tonnai to  (buoon!)

00:22:32.830 --> 00:22:36.290
nande konna ni mendo kusai ndesu ka~!

00:22:37.620 --> 00:22:42.290
(kokechatta)  omoi shatai o hikiokoshi

00:22:42.380 --> 00:22:46.800
(mou ikkai)  SUTAATO! doushite daro? waracchau

00:22:47.130 --> 00:22:55.350
(sou da yone!)  ikou yo! shisen no
saki ni wa tomodachi ga matteru kara!

00:22:56.100 --> 00:23:00.940
AKUSERU akeru to hirogatte iku SHIN!  (saikou no!)

00:23:00.940 --> 00:23:05.780
SUPIIDO APPU shichau kanjou wa mou tomanna~i!  (YEI!)

00:23:05.980 --> 00:23:10.490
marude hane ga haechatta mitai  (Wow!)

00:23:10.530 --> 00:23:13.070
GIA nante TOPPU koete motto agete

00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:17.500
"seishun TSUURINGU"  doko made icchau?

00:23:17.950 --> 00:23:19.750
buon!  buon!  buon!  buon!  buoon!

00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:22.540
hashiri dashichaeba iin janai?

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:24.590
buon!  buon!  buon!  buon!  buoon!

00:23:24.590 --> 00:23:27.510
todorokima~su, bakuon!!

00:23:29.920 --> 00:23:34.930
Next time on Bakuon!!
New Classmate!!

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.980
